            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of N-Oxyureas by Substitution and Cope-Type Hydroamination Reactions Using O-Isocyanate Precursors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6574-6577</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03288</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Oxy-carbamate O-isocyanate precursors facilitate access to synthetically valuable N-oxyureas via substitution with amines. This work exploits the reactivity of suitable O-isocyanate precursors, identified by a thorough study highlighting the different reactivity of isocyanate masking groups. This led to bench-stable O-isocyanate precursors, offering improved versatility in the synthesis of N-oxyureas, and demonstrates the controlled reactivity of masked O-isocyanates. Suitable precursors also enabled the first example of Cope-type hydroamination of unsaturated hydroxyureas.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
